			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
		<item>
		<title>TNA&#8217;s KC Navarro offers inspiration to kids dealing with bullying</title>
		<link>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398543-tnas-kc-navarro-offers-inspiration-to-kids-dealing-with-bullying/</link>
					<comments>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398543-tnas-kc-navarro-offers-inspiration-to-kids-dealing-with-bullying/#respond</comments>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alex Kahrs]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 23:20:18 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Featured Top Story]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Impact Wrestling News]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[KC Navarro]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[TNA]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[X-Division]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.wrestleview.com/?p=398543</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>In an interview with OutKick Dropkick, KC Navarro recounted a recent trip to El Paso, Texas, where he&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398543-tnas-kc-navarro-offers-inspiration-to-kids-dealing-with-bullying/">TNA&#8217;s KC Navarro offers inspiration to kids dealing with bullying</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In an interview with <a href="https://www.foxnews.com/outkick-sports/tna-kc-navarro-inspiring-message-young-kids-overcoming-bullying-chase-your-dream">OutKick Dropkick</a>, KC Navarro recounted a recent trip to El Paso, Texas, where he spoke to hundreds of kids at a wrestling tournament.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">On the message he shared, Navarro looked back to his own experience in overcoming bullying as a child:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Just when I asked them the first question, how many of you guys have been bullied before? The amount of hands that went up was so crazy. They&#8217;re younger, they&#8217;re in school, so they&#8217;re really gonna be able to relate to me when I say, hey, like, you know those tables at lunch, the really, really long ones that sit a lot of kids, they&#8217;re all like, yeah, yeah. I go, yeah, I sat by myself ‘cause no one wanted to sit with me ‘cause I wanted to wrestle. I wanted to be a wrestler and like their faces like they couldn&#8217;t believe that.</p>
</blockquote>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Navarro, who become Number One Contender to the TNA X-Division after a win at Destination X, encouraged the kids in attendance to chase their dreams no matter what, a message that appeared to resonate with the group:</p>



<blockquote class="wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Now I&#8217;m just like, yeah man, please chase your dream. It&#8217;s so important to chase your dreams, and I feel like there&#8217;s probably a lot of kids there that didn&#8217;t know who I was, but when I left, man, they were thanking me. Some kids had tears in their eyes because they were telling me like, ‘Man, I went through the same thing. I wanted to be something and like nobody wanted to be my friend and left me alone and I never thought somebody at your level would have gone through something like that.’ And I&#8217;m like, yeah, but I didn&#8217;t quit, you know, like you can&#8217;t quit. You have to believe in yourself.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398543-tnas-kc-navarro-offers-inspiration-to-kids-dealing-with-bullying/">TNA&#8217;s KC Navarro offers inspiration to kids dealing with bullying</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
					<wfw:commentRss>https://www.wrestleview.com/featured-top-story/398543-tnas-kc-navarro-offers-inspiration-to-kids-dealing-with-bullying/feed/</wfw:commentRss>
			<slash:comments>0</slash:comments>
		
		
			</item>
