					<description><![CDATA[<p>AEW Collision Thanksgiving Night ResultsNovember 26, 2026 (Taped 11/25)Ralston (Omaha), Nebraska (Liberty First Credit Union Arena)Results by: Alex&#8230;</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398441-aew-collision-thanksgiving-night-results-11-26-26-title-match-continental-classic-tournament-matches/">AEW Collision Thanksgiving Night Results &#8211; 11/26/26 (Title Match, Continental Classic Tournament Matches)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>AEW Collision <strong>Thanksgiving Night</strong></strong> <strong>Results</strong><br><strong>November 26, 2026</strong> <strong>(Taped 11/25)</strong><br><strong>Ralston (Omaha), Nebraska (Liberty First Credit Union Arena)</strong><br><strong>Results by: Alex Kahrs of Wrestleview.com</strong></p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Gobble gobble y&#8217;all&#8230;Thanksgiving night is alright for Collidin&#8217;!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Commentary welcomes us to the show, looking at the matches for tonight and the leaderboards for the Continental Classic. Before we get to those matches for tonight, we will kick things off with the World Trios Title on the line! Don Callis Family&#8217;s squad for this match make their entrance, followed by Swerve Strickland and The New Level to get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="aew-world-trios-championships-match-the-dangerous-new-level-defends-against-josh-alexander-rocky-romeo-and-hechicero" class="wp-block-heading">AEW World Trios Championships Match: The Dangerous New Level defends against Josh Alexander, Rocky Romeo and Hechicero</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Creed and Alexander start things off, trading offense until Austin gets the Walking Weapon down to the mat. He goes for a cover, but Josh bridges out at two before fighting to his feet. Alexander sent to the ropes, but he catches Creed with a slam to the mat before going for an ankle lock. Austin breaks free quickly, sweeping Josh&#8217;s leg out of his leg before making the tag to Kofi. Double-team by the New Level gets Kofi a nearfall.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">In comes Strickland with the tag, and a triple-team allows him to pick up a two count. He goes after Alexander in the corner, but Josh fights back before making a tag to Romero&#8230;who gets taken out with a suplex by Swerve! Hechicero comes in, but Strickland fends him off before sending Rocky back to the mat. He goes up top for an flying elbow to the back of Romero, only to be blindsided by Alexander. DCF go after the champs, but are sent to the outside for their troubles&#8230;leading to a triple dive by the Dangerous New Level, who return to the ring to a big pop as we go to ad break!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">DCF in control coming back from break, with Josh and Romero taking Creed down with a double suplex. The pair turn their attention to Swerve on the apron, with Alexander slamming him onto it before knocking him to the floor with a low cross body. Rocky has an opening to go after Creed, but is taken down as Josh gets back into the ring. Creed manages to send him to the mat as well, with both men down as Kofi reaches out for a tag. He gets the tag and so does Hechicero as the two go at it.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The luchador sends Kofi toward the corner with a catapult, but Kofi blocks it and takes Hechicero down. Romero tries to intervenen but is sent to the floor by Creed, but the distraction allows Hechicero to bend and twist Kofi into a pinning combination&#8230;only for Swerve to break up the pin!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Hechicero makes him pay for this, forcing him to the outside as Josh comes in off a tag. He gets Kofi in an ankle look as Rocky lands a missile dropkick on him, celebrating too early in the corner and taking a House Call from Strickland as a result. Swerve breaks up a pin attempt and Rocky is tagged in, only to take a Swerve Stomp allowing the champs to pick up the win and retain.</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-and-still-aew-world-trios-champions-the-dangerous-new-level" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall and still AEW World Trios Champions: The Dangerous New Level</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The champs celebrate as we get a promotional video for the Holidays on a New Level deal at ShopAEW, taking us right back to ringside for our next match. Sisters of Sin make their way to the ring as Nixi XS and A-Ray (Anna Ray to some) are already here before this match gets underway!</p>



<h3 id="the-sisters-of-sin-julia-hart-and-skye-blue-vs-nixi-xs-and-a-ray" class="wp-block-heading">The Sisters of Sin (Julia Hart and Skye Blue) vs. Nixi XS and A-Ray</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Blue and Nixi start things off, with Skye quickly taking control before tagging in Hart. The Sisters take out Ray before she can get in, and a double-team gets the Sisters of Sin a quick win.</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-the-sisters-of-sin" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall: The Sisters of Sin</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Thekla joins them in the ring to celebrate as we go backstage, where Marina Shafir addresses the Death Riders being down another man while Daniel Garcia recovers from injury. She also says that Mercedes Moné may have beaten her at Full Gear, but she didn&#8217;t dominate s&#8211;t&#8230;something the champ takes umbrage with, as she blindsides Shafir!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Moné is joined by The Cut, who go after the rest of the Riders in a brawl that makes its way to ringside. Wheeler Yuta and Ace Austin take their fight to the ring itself, where Austin gets Yuta set up for a 3:10 to Yuma&#8230;or as Nigel calls it, a 3:10 to Yuta! Moxley gets into the ring to go after the Gunns and Austin, but Finlay blindsides him as Connors joins in the beatdown.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We see Claudio Castagnoli arriving to the ring, only to be attacked by The Cut once he gets in the ring. He fights back with a double uppercut on the Gunns off the ropes, sending them out of the ring as Connors tries to psyche him out&#8230;to no avail! He gets sent out of the ring as well, and Ace narrowly avoids being swung around with a low blow to Claudio by Jay White. Shafir jumps on the Switchblade&#8217;s back, only to take a Backstabber by Moné! Claudio grabs the legs of the CEO, looking for a Giant Swing before The Cut stop him. They complete the beatdown and stand tall as we go to commercial break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We head to ringside for our next match, as Ricochet makes his entrance in this Continental Classic bout. Out next is Brody King as commentary talks about the match against Garcia, and with that we get underway!</p>



<h3 id="continental-classic-tournament-blue-league-match-ricochet-0-vs-brody-king-3" class="wp-block-heading">Continental Classic Tournament Blue League Match: Ricochet (0) vs. Brody King (3)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">King takes Ricochet to the mat, only for Ricochet to immediately roll out of the ring for safety. He gets back in, and is immediately sent down hard to the canvas. Ricochet takes another breather on the outside before returning to the ring&#8230;where Brody takes him right back down. Ricochet fights out of a suplex, but takes a shoulder tackle from King before dodging a senton.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Both men are on their feet as Ricochet tries to take King down with some chops to no avail, before sending him over and to the outside. He mocks Brody from behind, something that he quickly pays for as King sends him crashing onto the announce table. He then sets up a chair by the barricade, and sends Ricochet into it before nearly crushing him with a cross body as we go to ad break!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We coem back as Brody goes for a German suplex, but Ricochet lands on his feet. The two meet at the corner, fighting it out on the turnbuckle before Ricochet breaks free for a kick knocking Brody down. He goes after King but is caught by the big man, who sends him to the corner. Ricochet fights back, but takes a chop to the chest that sends him down hard.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ricochet gets to his feet in the corner, catching King with a fall away slam sending him into the turnbuckle. He goes back after Brody, sweeping him off his feet for a shooting star press and a two count. Brody fights back, sending Ricochet crashing to the canvas for a nearfall of his own.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ricochet gets to the corner as Brody pauses for just a moment before going for a cannonball, and this allows Ricochet to dodge it as ten minutes remain. King fights back looking for a Baldo Bomb, but Ricochet escapes&#8230;only to be dropped down by the big man anyway! Brody builds up some steam with a knee to Ricochet in the corner, catching him with a cannonball. Ricochet wriggles out of his grip following this, landing a Spirit Gun and a Hidden Blade of sorts to keep the big man down for a second Spirit Gun, followed by the 630 for the win!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-ricochet-3" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall: Ricochet (3)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Show of respect between King and Ricochet following the bout, as we get some hype for Konosuke Takeshita taking on Bandido soon enough. Before we get that, we hear from &#8220;Jungle&#8221; Jack Perry as he addresses his second loss to Samoa Joe&#8230;and those who have had his back all this time, saying he&#8217;s one step closer to achieving his dream. He&#8217;s this close to doing what some are saying is impossible&#8230;he&#8217;s going to be World Champion, just you wait.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With that, we head back to ringside as Konosuke Takeshita makes his entrance for our next match. The Alpha looks to pick up the slack after coming in to replace the injured Daniel Garcia, and out next is Bandido to get this match underway!</p>



<h3 id="continental-classic-blue-league-match-bandido-3-vs-konosuka-takeshita-0" class="wp-block-heading">Continental Classic Blue League Match: Bandido (3) vs. Konosuka Takeshita (0)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">There&#8217;s a back and forth between both men to start things off, leading to each man looking to take the other out with a suplex. Exchange of arm drags before Bandido hits the ropes, only to be taken out with a shoulder tackle. Cover by Takeshita gets a two count, and both men trade nearfalls before Bandido rolls out of the ring as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Takeshita hoisted up by the luchador as we come back, and the ROH World Champion lands some kicks before being sent to the corner by the Alpha&#8230;only to take him down hard for a two count! Takeshita in the corner as Bandido lands a boot to the face, but the Alpha fights back for a Blue Thunder Bomb and a nearfall of his own. Bandido dodges a knee strike before hitting the ropes, but he struggles to take him down before they end up sending each other to the mat wth a double down.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ref begins the count as both men slowly start to move. They make it back to their feet, with each trying to send the other back down&#8230;and Bandido wins out as he sets up for a 21 Plex!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">NO! Takeshita holds onto the ropes, driving the luchador into them to stop the momentum. The two start slugging it out on the apron as ten minutes remain. This goes back and forth until they resort to trying to send each other onto the hardest part of the ring&#8230;with Bandido sending the Alpha to the floor with a headscissors as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Coming back from break, Bandido sends Takeshita to the outside for a dive as five minutes remain in the match. He brings the Alpha back into the ring, favoring his arm as he goes for a frog splash off the top&#8230;but it&#8217;s only good for two as Konosuke kicks out!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The two get to their feet, and decide on a duel of sorts as they pace toward the opposite corners before trading strikes in the center&#8230;until Takeshita sends the luchador crashing down with a powerbomb for two! Bandido sets up for a 21 Plex, but the Alpha blocks him for a tombstone piledriver. Pendulum pickup is reversed, and Bandido gets a two count. Another trade of offense and this time it&#8217;s Konosuke with the nearfall, before both men take each other out with a kick.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Both men are down, slowly stirring as they get to their feet once more. Bandido with some forearm strikes, but gets leveled by Konosuke&#8230;who follows up with a big knee from the corner for two. One minute remains as Takeshita goes back to the corner, invoking the spirit of Garcia with a slight dance before charging at him with the Raging Fire&#8230;only to be cradled by Bandido for two! 30 seconds left as Bandido gets taken out by Takeshita, and we get to 15 as Bandido fights back for a 21 Plex&#8230;as the bell rings for the time limit draw!</p>



<h3 id="match-ends-in-a-time-limit-draw-each-man-earns-1-point" class="wp-block-heading">Match ends in a Time Limit Draw (each man earns 1 point)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The two men show respect after a hard-fought battle, before we get a video package hyping up Maya World and Hyan taking on Britt Baker and Persephone next Saturday on Collision (which, yes, we&#8217;re still getting a Collision on Saturday after the 3-hour combo on Wednesday lol).</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With that, we head back to ringside where Don Callis (and his stinky ahh &#8220;music&#8221;) makes his way out. He talks about wanting to get an answer from the AEW National Champion, claiming we&#8217;re about to have Ilja Dragunov join his Family.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">With that, Dragunov makes his entrance to a nice pop from the crowd. Don Callis asks the champ how it feels standing across the ring from him, before explaining that it&#8217;s as simple as giving a yes or no answer. Before we get that, however, Callis mentions that he is willing to double his initial talent contract offer, before presenting a check from his own bank account&#8230;revealing his offer is now TRIPLE what he initially offered. It&#8217;s more than he&#8217;s ever offered a talent in recruiting them.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He commends Dragunov for being a smart businessman, and says he not only gets the money but 24-hour access to Don himself. He then presents the question of whether Dragunov is a smart man&#8230;will he join the Don Callis Family? The fans are chanting for the champ to say no&#8230;but the champ says yes.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This gets boos as Dragunov says yes, he is a very smart man&#8230;which is why the answer to his other question is no, he will NOT join the Don Callis Family! He rips up the check to a big pop from the crowd, his music playing as Don leaves the ring incensed.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We get a graphic for our upcoming matches before going to commercial.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">We head back to ringside as the Kasper Brothers make their entrance. They make a beeline for the ring with their opponents Atlas Armstrong and Talon Graves already in the ring as we get things underway!</p>



<h3 id="kasper-brothers-vs-atlas-armstrong-and-talon-graves" class="wp-block-heading">Kasper Brothers vs. Atlas Armstrong and Talon Graves</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Jacob quickly goes to work on&#8230;one of these guys (Talon I think), sending him to the outside where Drew gets the pounce on him. He sends Graves to his own corner, where Atlas gets the tag for a right hand that does not faze Jacob one bit.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Armstrong tries to live up to his namesake with another right hand, but gets sent to the corner instead. Jacob with a superplex and a tag to Drew&#8230;setting up for a Kasper Cannonball to pick up the win in short order.</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-kasper-brothers" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall: Kasper Brothers</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Drew goes after Talon after the match for a moment as we look ahead to the 8-Man Tag now official for next Wednesday. Backstage, the Brawling Birds address Wrathlander as they have their sights set on winning their tag titles back&#8230;but first, they want to have a chat with the champs.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, Athena and Billie Starkz make their way out for our next match. Commentary hypes the ROH Women&#8217;s Title match for Final Battle, which will see Athena defend against Hyan. Mina Shirakawa makes her entrance next, followed by Queen Aminata as the pair head to the ring to get things underway!</p>



<h3 id="athena-and-billie-starkz-vs-queen-aminata-and-mina-shirakawa" class="wp-block-heading">Athena and Billie Starkz vs. Queen Aminata and Mina Shirakawa</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The four women stand off as Athena mocks Aminata, only for the TBS Champion to be blindsided by Billie to get the match started. Aminata fires back with a short arm lariat followed by a suplex, with Mina tagging in to keep on the attack. Starkz breaks free for a tag to Athena, but the ROH Women&#8217;s Champion is sent to the corner. Athena fights back, but in comes Aminata off the tag to send Starkz off the apron.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Billie comes back into the ring, but she and Athena get set up for a pair of Chocolate Kisses from both the Queen and Shirakawa as we go to ad break.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Mina takes Billie down hard for a two count as we come back, only for Starkz to counter a figure four leglock for a nearfall of her own. Tag made to Athena, who takes Mina to the mat with a release German suplex. Mina gets to the corner, where she takes a handspring elbow from Shirakawa. Aminata comes in to intervene, but is fended off by the &#8220;Forever Champion&#8221; who makes the tag to Starkz. Double-team leads to a nearfall before Mina manages to kick out.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Aminata comes in and the two take out Athena, sending her to the outside. Billie sends the Queen to the floor with a dive through the ropes, but is dropped down to the floor herself thanks to a diving cross body by Mina! She brings Billie back into the ring for a headscissors takedown, calling for Aminata to go up top.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The ref argues with the Queen about this, allowing Athena to take Mina out with the O Face before Billie makes the cover for the win.</p>



<h3 id="winners-via-pinfall-athena-and-billie-starkz" class="wp-block-heading">Winners via pinfall: Athena and Billie Starkz</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The pair celebrate as we get confirmation that Queen Aminata will defend the TBS Championship against Billie Starkz this Wednesday. Up next is our main event as Tommaso Ciampa takes on Nick Wayne in Gold League action for the Continental Classic!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-Commercial Break-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Back at ringside, we&#8217;re asked to &#8220;drop some W&#8217;s in the chat&#8221; for Nick Wayne as he makes his entrance, reminding us of the news that Nick Wayne&#8230;beat Chris Jericho&#8230;(Pyro goes off)&#8230;twice. He says he&#8217;s also the fan favorite to win the Continental Classic. He starts to talk some more smack about winsmaxxing and mogging Ciampa to oblivion, saying he will remind everyone that&#8211;never mind all that, as Tommaso Ciampa makes his entrance. With both men in the ring, we get this main event underway!</p>



<h3 id="continental-classic-gold-league-match-tommaso-ciampa-0-vs-nick-wayne-3" class="wp-block-heading">Continental Classic Gold League Match: Tommaso Ciampa (0) vs. Nick Wayne (3)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ciampa quickly goes on the attack, laying into Wayne until he tries to back off&#8230;only to spit gum in the face of Tommaso! This riles up the Psycho Killer, who chases him out of the ring and sends Nick into the barricade. He brings Nick back into the ring, but this allows Wayne to fight back before hitting the ropes&#8230;where he gets dropped to the mat with a dropkick by Ciampa!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">He sends Wayne to the outside, allowing the Prodigy to do some unintentional restmaxxing. Ciampa leaves the ring, setting Nick up on a chair by the barricade&#8230;but Wayne fights back once again, sending the former National Champion crashing into the guardrail as we go to ad break!</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">-FULL AD BREAK (ON HBO MAX)-</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Wayne maintains control back in the ring, only to regret posemaxxing when Ciampa sends him into the ropes. Nick hits the ropes himself, only to be knocked down by Tommaso who follows up with a Psycho Driller for a nearfall. Nick fights back for a jawbreaker before the fight reaches the apron, where Ciampa drops him onto the hardest part of the ring.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Ciampa favoring his injured knee as Wayne tries to recover in the ring. The ref checks on Tommaso before starting a count, which is answered by Ciampa returning to the apron&#8230;only to take a dropkick to the knee by Wayne! Nick sends him to the mat before going for a 450 splash, getting a nearfall as ten minutes remain.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nick goes for a figure four leglock, attacking the injured knee some more as Ciampa struggles toward the ropes. He reaches the bottom rope to force a break, but not before Nick attacks the knee some more before backing off. Nick starts mocking Ciampa as he gets to his feet, only to take a series of chops from Tommaso.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Nick connects with a thrust kick, but Ciampa is back up as he takes Nick out with a Psycho Driller&#8230;but a pin is countered as Wayne gets a nearfall instead! Down goes the knee pad as Nick tries to go for a Wayne&#8217;s World&#8230;only to be hit with a knee by Ciampa, who picks up the win and his first 3 points!</p>



<h3 id="winner-via-pinfall-tommaso-ciampa-3" class="wp-block-heading">Winner via pinfall: Tommaso Ciampa (3)</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Not much celebration going on as Ciampa struggles to stay standing, favoring his knee some more as Thanksgiving Collision comes to a close.</p>



<h3 id="quick-results" class="wp-block-heading">Quick Results:</h3>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>AEW World Trios Championships Match:</strong> The Dangerous New Level def. Josh Alexander, Rocky Romeo and Hechicero</li>



<li>The Sisters of Sin (Julia Hart and Skye Blue) def. Nixi XS and A-Ray</li>



<li><strong>Continental Classic Tournament Blue League Match:</strong> Ricochet (3) def. Brody King (3)</li>



<li><strong>Continental Classic Blue League Match:</strong> Bandido (4) vs. Konosuka Takeshita (1) ends in a Time Limit Draw</li>



<li>Kasper Brothers def. Atlas Armstrong and Talon Graves</li>



<li>Athena and Billie Starkz def. Queen Aminata and Mina Shirakawa</li>



<li><strong>Continental Classic Gold League Match:</strong> Tommaso Ciampa (3) def. Nick Wayne (3)</li>
</ul>
<p>The post <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com/top-story/398441-aew-collision-thanksgiving-night-results-11-26-26-title-match-continental-classic-tournament-matches/">AEW Collision Thanksgiving Night Results &#8211; 11/26/26 (Title Match, Continental Classic Tournament Matches)</a> appeared first on <a href="https://www.wrestleview.com">WWE News, WWE Results, AEW News, AEW Results</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
